Everything under this directory comes from the Penn World Table (PWT),
releases 8.0, 8.1, 9.0, 9.1, 10.0, 10.01 and 11.0, published by the
Groningen Growth and Development Centre (GGDC), University of Groningen, at
https://www.rug.nl/ggdc/productivity/pwt/ (earlier releases at
https://www.rug.nl/ggdc/productivity/pwt/earlier-releases), and for 11.0 and
10.01 on DataverseNL (https://doi.org/10.34894/FABVLR,
https://doi.org/10.34894/QT5BCC).

Each release page, read on 2026-10-05, says that the release ("Penn World
Table 11.0" and so on) "by Robert C. Feenstra, Robert Inklaar and Marcel P.
Timmer is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
License", and asks, under "Attribution requirement":

  When using these data (for whatever purpose), please make the following
  reference: Feenstra, Robert C., Robert Inklaar and Marcel P. Timmer
  (2015), "The Next Generation of the Penn World Table" American Economic
  Review, 105(10), 3150-3182, available for download at www.ggdc.net/pwt

The DataverseNL records of 11.0 and 10.01 state CC BY 4.0 as well.

The files under raw/<release>/ are GGDC's own files, byte for byte; each
release's MANIFEST.json records their URLs, sizes, sha256 and
Last-Modified. The program packages among them contain input data from
other sources as PWT distributes them; the terms of those inputs were not
checked.

The Parquet under parquet/<release>/ was made from the Stata (.dta) files:

  - for 8.0 and 8.1, the Stata file inside the release's zip was read
  - columns were typed by name: identifiers as text, year as an integer,
    the measures as 64-bit floats (4-byte floats widened exactly)
  - codes with Stata value labels (i_cig, i_xm, i_xr, i_outlier, i_irr and
    the coded columns of labor_detail) were replaced by their labels, the
    text PWT's own xlsx files show
  - Stata missing values and empty strings became NULL
  - the strings of pwt81.dta were decoded as Mac Roman
  - rows keep the order of the Stata file
  - no other value was changed

The code that fetches, checks and converts is in the repository this
dataset was built from and does not apply here.
